<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.11.3: Modeling with Exponential Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01446</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.11.3: Modeling with Exponential Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2bf57462-b28c-4596-8b73-28d269dfb520</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Your teacher will give your group three different kinds of balls.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Your goal is to measure the rebound heights, model the relationship between the number of bounces and the heights,
  and compare the bounciness of the balls.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
        
          <media alt="Group of different types of sport balls.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_13_06_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Create a table similar to the one below and begin your investigation. Make sure to note which ball goes with
        which column.</para>
